# GitHub Actions Conventions

## Workflow Purpose

`build_release.yaml` — runs on every push to `main` and on `workflow_dispatch`.
It executes the Go updater (`make run`) and commits the refreshed formula back to `main`.

## Permissions

Grant only the minimum required permissions. The formula-update workflow needs:
```yaml
permissions:
  contents: write  # to push the updated formula
```
Do not add `packages`, `id-token`, or `pull-requests` unless there is a specific need.

## Pinning Actions

Pin third-party actions to a full commit SHA for security, or at minimum to a major version tag:
```yaml
# ✅ major version tag (acceptable)
uses: actions/checkout@v5

# ✅ full SHA (preferred for security)
uses: actions/checkout@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683
```

## Go Setup

Always specify the exact Go version to match `go.mod`:
```yaml
- uses: actions/setup-go@v5
  with:
    go-version: "1.23.4"
```

## Commit Bot Identity

The auto-commit step must use a bot identity, not a personal account:
```yaml
git config user.name "GitHub Actions"
git config user.email "actions@github.com"
```

## Secrets

Use `${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}` for repo-scoped operations. Never hard-code tokens.
